<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Emmeram</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Emmeram of Regensburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Emmeram was a Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> who worked as a missionary in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> and was martyred in the 7th century. His tomb at Regensburg became the site of a Benedictine abbey named after him, whose abbots were for long also bishops of Regensburg. The abbey later became an imperial principality within the city walls and is now part of the palace of the Thurn und Taxis family.</p></div>
